  "changes": [
    "SQLite VACUUM INTO snapshots capture committed WAL state, preserve exact SQL values and historical records, and validate integrity, foreign keys, and contiguous known migration history.",
    "Export and import publish only into a new private directory with no replacement. Copy checks size and SHA256. Publication and later durability errors have separate result state.",
    "MySQL reconciliation requires the exact embedded migration digest, pending intent, actor, operation ID, and independent evidence digest. Applied or reverted decisions record an audit receipt and clear intent in one owned transaction.",
    "Exact retries are idempotent. Conflicting decisions, unknown digests, failed audit writes, and nontransactional control tables refuse completion. The operation does not repair DDL itself.",
    "MySQL migration control tables require InnoDB. Existing MyISAM tables fail closed instead of pretending to commit audit and completion atomically."
  ],
